{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Big Argument", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Coming to a Compromise", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 9, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals For Possibility, Certainty, Suggestions and Expectations", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use modals when you want to express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use/Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Form\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"might<br> can/could <br> may\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To express possibility in the past, present or future <br> *<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can</span> is only used to talk about the present and future (not the past)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>might / might not + verb</li><li>could / could not + verb</li><li>may / may not + verb</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Peter <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> be quite dopey sometimes.<br/>You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">might</span> be right about that.<br/>I guess I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> let go of my controlling habits.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To express that something is necessarily true\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"must (not) + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">She <span class=\\\"strong\\\">must</span> have felt like he didn't care about her. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"should <br> could <br> might  <br>would\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To express suggestions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"modal + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You <span class=\\\"strong\\\">should</span> come to a compromise.<br/>That <span class=\\\"strong\\\">would</span> be a good place to start, don't you think?<br/>He<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> should</span> have done it a while ago.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"supposed to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"To express expectation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"supposed to + verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'm <span class=\\\"strong\\\">supposed to</span> interview a few applicants next week.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Negative Questions To Encourage Agreement", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Negative questions are another way to confirm information you already know. Using a variety of structures gives your speaking a more sophisticated feel. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Negative questions can begin with the structures: <br> <br> <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think ... ? <br>Isn't it right that ... ? <br> You don't think ... ? <br>Wouldn't it be better if ... ? <br>Doesn't that mean ... ?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Don't you think you should come to a compromise?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You don't think you should take a step back, perhaps? ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take a toll", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make someone's situation worse in a gradual way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being the manager of a trendy place takes a toll on your social life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about feelings and reactions.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dopey", "type": "name"}, {"content": "slow and confused", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter didn't realize Camilla had a crush on him. He can be quite dopey sometimes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to follow in someone's footsteps", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be inspired by someone to do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: His love life is successful. Maybe I should follow in his footsteps.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "sensible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "reasonable and wise", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I should hire an assistant manager. <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: That sounds like a sensible idea.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "convinced", "type": "name"}, {"content": "completely certain about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm not convinced that hiring an assistant manager will solve my problem.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "controlling", "type": "name"}, {"content": "dominating and commanding the actions of someone else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I guess I could let go of my controlling habits ...", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le01ob09re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Make profiles of your classmates and put them in a pile.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Get three profiles of other classmates.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Try to convince your partner that one of the profiles is the right person for them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use encouraging agreement language and feeling and sensation language. \u201cHe seems like ... \u201d to convince your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about feelings and sensations.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I  express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I encourage agreement. ", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about feelings and sensations.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can encourage agreement. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " How stressed out are you by work or school?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Do you think